{"name":"Lemon Juice","hex":"#ffffec","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lemon juice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The liquid extract of lemon fruit, notably sour and often condensed, as used especially in food preparation.","The juice of a sweet lemon or sweet lime."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon_juice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Juice","blocks":[{"text":"Juice is a drink made from the extraction or pressing of the natural liquid contained in fruit and vegetables. It can also refer to liquids that are flavored with concentrate or other biological food sources like meat or seafood, such as clam juice. Juice is commonly consumed as a beverage or used as an ingredient or flavoring in foods or other beverages, such as smoothies. Juice emerged as a popular beverage choice after the development of pasteurization methods enabled its preservation without using fermentation. The largest fruit juice consumers are New Zealand and Colombia. Fruit juice consumption on average increases with a country's income level."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Orange_juice_1.jpg/330px-Orange_juice_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juice","wikidata":"Q8492"},{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/330px-Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2720565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg/250px-Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg/500px-Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg/250px-Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG/250px-Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG/500px-Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG/250px-Citrus_limon_-_Lemon_tree_-_Limonero_-_Limoeiro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w